body: |-
  ## Plan output
  - Schema-locked authority.yaml ships at v6.0.4 (no read tools, just write). Three trigger paths: shift-nominate, shift-adopt-default, migration-on-upgrade.
  - Stop-hook surgical wraps: roster-detection helper after line 68; Check 6 (lines 405-435) wrap emission; Check 10 (lines 566-585) wrap emission ABOVE line 575 only. Lines 873-886 (compliance-history.jsonl) stay UNCONDITIONAL — Loid's data continuity surface.
  - Doctor adds `'info'` CheckResult status with `⠂` icon, dim suffix `(no claimant active)`. Slot after Portal compliance, before flows.yaml.
  - shift.ts adds Step 2c-nominate-compliance for cohort C only (existing project + no compliance + ~aspect lines exist). Default Y, --no-prompt for CI.
  - CLAUDE.md reframe — "Rune owns symbol enforcement when rostered" + clarify framework still blocks on missing .purpose / portal gates / lore-required (general hygiene, not symbol policy).

  ## Cohort analysis (Jinx)
  - A: compliance rostered → zero risk
  - B: no compliance + no aspects → zero risk (short-circuits)
  - C: no compliance + has aspects → REAL RISK, silent enforcement loss. Migration notice mitigates.

  ## Test cases
  10 regression cases enumerated, covering both compliance-rostered and absent paths, edge cases (zero aspects, zero components), CI behavior.

  ## Sequence
  Wave 1 foundation (parallel) → Wave 2 de-enforcement (critical path) → Wave 3 surfacing → Wave 4 docs → Wave 5 tests → Wave 6 release.

  ## 4 open user questions
  1. paradigm-mcp version bump: 6.0.4 (synchronized) or stay 6.0.3 (no MCP change)?
  2. Migration-notice copy tone — direct enough?
  3. Locate `paradigm compliance-check` source file (Architect couldn't verify path)
  4. authority.yaml location: `.paradigm/authority.yaml` or nested under `.paradigm/agents/`?

  ## Out of scope (16 items pushed to v6.1/v6.2)
  Soft-block primitive, authority MCP tools, hook-orchestrator, compliance-check→aspect-report rename, new Rune MCP tools, session-start ambient pass for Rune, notebook tier split, Rune's 6 transferable patterns, optout/severity registries, JSONLogic predicates, override-cluster coaching, per-component snapshots, Auto-author/Guard behaviors, 316-anchor drift remediation.
